    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=199721": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Petroleum Engineering and Geology",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Chair, Department of Petroleum Engineering and Geology Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Chair, Department of Petroleum Engineering and Geology Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Chair, Department of Petroleum Engineering and Geology Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Advancement Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Apr 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 199721 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: Marietta College invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Petroleum Engineering and Geology.  This is a full time (9-month), tenure-eligible or tenure track faculty position to begin no later than January 2027. The Petroleum Engineering program at Marietta College is accredited by the EAC of ABET.  The faculty and staff of the Department consist of four engineers and two geologists who are committed to collaborating across programs and areas of study. As the only Petroleum Engineering Program housed in a small, private college, the department seeks candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching in the spirit of a broad liberal arts education. We value the mentoring of undergraduate students, teaching excellence, experiential learning, and the professional development of our students. The Department offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Petroleum Engineering and Geology, as well as undergraduate minors in Energy Systems, Geology, and Petroleum Engineering.  In addition, the Geology faculty support an inter-disciplinary Environmental Science program. The Petroleum Engineering program currently enrolls approximately 60 students, and Geology enrolls about 25.  A priority for the new Chair will be to partner actively across campus and within the industry to support program growth and student retention and success. Marietta College seeks an experienced petroleum engineer who is dynamic, enthusiastic, and preferably has a proven record of collaboration and excellence in Petroleum Engineering education. Responsibilities of this position include: Comprehensive departmental organization and administration Accreditation maintenance and continuous program improvement Partnership with the admissions team to support program recruitment and enrollment Support student success and retention Fiscal management, budget and grant development Mentorship and evaluation of faculty Scholarly activities Coordination of the Department's Industry Advisory Committee Facilitation of student placement in internships and full-time positions through an industry network Active engagement with the Society of Petroleum Engineers and industry partners Service to the college and community. The Department Chair reports directly to the Provost of the College. This is a full-time (9-month) position with an additional stipend paid for Chair duties and modest summer duties. Requirements: Applicants must be a graduate of an accredited petroleum engineering program, have significant industry experience and connections, and hold an advanced degree in petroleum engineering or a closely related engineering or science discipline. The program has teaching needs in production engineering and completions; the new hire must be able to provide this expertise. Teaching or instructional experience or demonstrated traits necessary to develop into a good teacher is preferred as is professional engineering registration. Additional Information: While professional development and scholarly achievements are valued, the primary focus of the Marietta College faculty is on undergraduate education, including classroom instruction, student advising, and student mentoring. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195423": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Earth Science (9-month, non-tenure track)",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Earth Science (9-month, non-tenure track) Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Earth Science (9-month, non-tenure track) Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Earth Science (9-month, non-tenure track) Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of Earth, Environmental, and Planetary Sciences Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Dec 8, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 195423 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: The Department of Earth, Environmental and Planetary Sciences at Marietta College invites applications for a 9-month, non-tenure track Assistant Professor position in Environmental Geology and Geographic Information Systems (GIS) beginning August 2026.  We welcome applications from candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: hydrology, GIS, environmental science, low-temperature geochemistry, geological engineering, natural hazards and risk assessment, and geomorphology.  The ideal candidate would have a proven track record of undergraduate, field-based teaching, and involvement of undergraduate students in research. Our class sizes are small and field-based learning is encouraged and supported; opportunities to lead travel courses with students are also available. Research with undergraduate students is also expected and supported. The university's location at the confluence of the Ohio and Muskingum rivers is ideal for environmental geology projects, and it is expected the candidate would utilize this resource in their courses and research.  The expected teaching duties will be 12 credits hours per semester. Marietta College recently formed the Center for Earth, Energy, and Environment, and it is anticipated that the selected candidate would play a key role in enhancing environmental science in the center.  Marietta College is also home to the only petroleum engineering program at a small liberal arts college, and the candidate's ability to contribute to curriculum involving energy and engineering would be welcome.  Review of applications will begin January 15th and continue until the position is filled. Requirements: Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Geology or a closely related field.  Preference will be given to candidates with a Ph.D., but candidates who are ABD will also be considered. Proficiency with GIS. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the undergraduate level, and incorporation of undergraduates in research. Past involvement in Environmental Science degree programs, or other closely related interdisciplinary programs, and associated curricular development. Proven expertise in hydrology and geological engineering. Ability to secure external funding to support undergraduate research. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, teaching statement (limit 2 pages), and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204234": {
      "title": "Program Director, Master of Business Administration",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Program Director, Master of Business Administration Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Program Director, Master of Business Administration Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Director, Master of Business Administration Category: Senior Executive Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business & Economics Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204234 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: Marietta College invites applications for the founding Program Director of its new Master of Business Administration (MBA) program, with an anticipated start date of January 2027. This is a full-time, administrative position with teaching responsibilities, commensurate with qualifications, reporting to the Provost of the College. The Program Director will serve as the academic, operational, relational, and student-services hub of the MBA, the first point of contact for prospective students, the coordinator of adjunct faculty, the steward of employer partnerships, and the lead on ACBSP candidacy documentation. For the right candidate, this is an uncommon opportunity: a small institution's culture and resources, with a genuinely new program to build from the ground up. Essential Functions: Curriculum and Academic Oversight: Coordinate academic scheduling, Canvas course maintenance, and instructional continuity across all five 8-week terms. Teaching: Teach one or more MBA courses annually within the Director's area of expertise. Adjunct Faculty Recruitment and Coordination: Recruit, onboard, and support qualified adjunct instructors, including orientation to shared course playbooks, Canvas shells, and AI Integration assignment standards. Student Services and Enrollment Management: Serve as the primary point of contact for all MBA inquiries from initial interest through graduation. Partner with Admissions and institutional stakeholders to steward the enrollment pipeline and cohort viability thresholds. Employer Partnerships and Alumni Engagement: Build employer and alumni partnerships supporting tuition reimbursement, corporate cohorts, and applied AI enabled capstone projects. Accreditation (ACBSP): Lead the ACBSP Candidacy Application process from Intent to Apply through self-study preparation and site visit. Maintain ACBSP Standard 5 faculty qualification tables annually. Service: Represent the MBA program in departmental, Graduate Council, and institutional service contexts. Requirements: Required Qualifications Master's degree in a business-related field is required at minimum. An MBA is acceptable as the qualifying degree for this position and satisfies the ACBSP minimum faculty credential for graduate business instruction. Minimum of three years of professional business experience outside of teaching. ACBSP Standard 5 requires documented in-field professional experience for all business unit faculty; this documentation must be on file before any instruction begins. Demonstrated ability to build and manage relationships with external stakeholders, including employers, alumni, or community organizations. Strong written and oral communication skills, including comfort presenting to faculty governance bodies, employer partners, and prospective students. Preferred Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D., D.B.A., or equivalent) in business, management, economics, or a closely related field is strongly preferred. Because the Program Director is expected to teach in the MBA program, a doctoral credential is the most straightforward way to support the program's ACBSP Standard 5 Doctorate Degree Qualified (DDQ) threshold. Demonstrated experience integrating artificial intelligence (AI) tools or methodologies into graduate level teaching or curriculum design. Prior graduate-level teaching experience, including experience with asynchronous online course delivery via Canvas LMS or a comparable platform. Experience coordinating or supervising adjunct or part-time faculty. Prior involvement in regional or professional accreditation processes (ACBSP, AACSB, HLC, or equivalent). Experience managing a student recruitment or enrollment pipeline,or developing employer tuition-reimbursement or corporate cohort partnerships. Familiarity with ACBSP accreditation standards,or demonstrated willingness to complete ACBSP mentor-supported candidacy training within the first year of appointment. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
