    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200562": {
      "title": "Multi-Skilled Trades (Carpentry, Painting, Masonry) & Assistant Locksmith",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Multi-Skilled Trades (Carpentry, Painting, Masonry) & Assistant Locksmith Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Multi-Skilled Trades (Carpentry, Painting, Masonry) & Assistant Locksmith Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Multi-Skilled Trades (Carpentry, Painting, Masonry) & Assistant Locksmith Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: May 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 200562 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: The multi-skilled trades/locksmith assistant will utilize a variety of specialized skills to fabricate, maintain, and repair the structural components of Marietta College and assist in maintaining the key system campus wide. Essential Functions of the Position: Fabricate or repair doors, windows, floors, ceilings, and other campus structures and grounds by sawing, cutting, planning, filing, bending, and drilling. Apply the principles of related crafts such as roofing, concrete placement, plastering, tile setting, and other trades need to maintain the campus. Use hand tools such as trowels, straight edges, plumb lines, wire cutters, etc. Repair and install drywall and finish small projects. Paint various classrooms, offices, doors, and outdoor projects on campus. Assist locksmith in maintaining the key system (Insta-Key System) for the security and safety of the campus. Learn the online operating system to maintain an accurate and up-to-date record of all keys, assignment of keys to personnel, lock hardware installations, keys issued to departments, and inventory of keys. Install new locks and door hardware as needed. Disassemble locks and replace worn tumblers, springs, and other parts as needed. Repair and adjust door-mounted closures, maintain hinges, and all related door hardware. Follow purchasing guidelines to buy materials and/or tools and equipment. Assist other trades and unskilled workers as needed during peak periods e.g. graduation, periods of extreme weather situations, and unexpected situations impacting campus. Assist in moving, setup, and teardown of special events and permanent or temporary offices. Assist with snow and ice removal as needed during major snow events. Requirements: Required Skills and Abilities: Skilled in the proper use of hand tools, power tools, and safety equipment. Demonstrated knowledge to perform emergency repairs in several fields. Ability to effectively communicate orally, in writing, or electronically. Ability to effectively work individually or in teams as well as with diverse groups without close supervision. Must be organized with the ability to prioritize work to ensure maximum efficiency. Must be able to use a computer to access email, work orders, and submit time for payroll processing. Required Experience & Education: Must have a minimum of a high school diploma or equivalent. Two years' experience performing facilities trades as described above in an institutional or commercial setting and/or career center or trades school. Must have a valid driver's license and an acceptable driving record. Additional Information: Physical Requirements: Ability to climb a ladder frequently and work in tight spaces occasionally. Ability to use small power tools and hand tools. Ability to carry up to 50 lbs. occasionally. Sufficient physical dexterity to bend, stoop, and climb to perform the duties of the job. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198068": {
      "title": "Director of Admission",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Director of Admission Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Admission Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Admission Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Admissions Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Mar 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 198068 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu . Job Description: The Director of Admission serves as a senior leader within the Enrollment Management Division and plays a critical role in shaping and executing a strategic recruitment and enrollment plan aligned with the institution's mission, goals, and financial sustainability.  This position provides operational and visionary leadership to the Office of Admission and supports cross-functional initiatives across the enrollment funnel, including recruitment, yield, marketing, data analytics, and transfer and access pipelines. The Director of Admissions reports directly to the Vice President of Enrollment Management. Essential Functions of the Position: Strategic Leadership and Planning Assists with the development and execution of a comprehensive undergraduate recruitment plan, utilizing data-informed decision-making, demographic trend analysis, and market research to drive enrollment growth and diversity. Partners with the VPEM to develop and assess multi-year enrollment strategies that align with institutional goals, retention initiatives, and revenue expectations. Operational Oversight Directs all aspects of the undergraduate recruitment cycle from inquiry to matriculation, including first-year, transfer, and special populations (e.g., adult learners, CCP dual enrollment). Manages and innovates the College's Transfer processes and oversees recruitment strategies specific to transfer students. Supervises the Tuition Exchange Program, including applicant education, documentation, and compliance monitoring. Supervision and Staff Development Provides direct supervision, coaching, and professional development to the admission team, with particular emphasis on admission counselors. Fosters a high-performance culture grounded in accountability, collaboration, inclusive excellence, and continuous improvement. Cross-Divisional Collaboration Collaborates with Marketing and Communication, Academic Affairs, Athletics, Financial Aid, and Student Life to create seamless, student-centered experiences across the enrollment pipeline. Contributes to the alignment of CRM, AI, and communication strategies to personalize outreach and improve yield. Data and Technology Integration Leverages CRM systems, analytics tools, and performance dashboards to monitor progress toward enrollment targets, optimize territory management, and assess ROI on recruitment initiatives. Collaborates with the VPEM and institutional research staff to interpret technical and statistical data to support strategic planning, institutional reporting, and forecasting. Institutional Representation and Visibility Represents the College at regional and national conferences, recruitment fairs, and community events, acting as a compelling ambassador of the institution's mission, values, and offerings. Serves on key campus committees and collaborates with faculty and staff on enrollment-related policies and initiatives. Acts as the chief admission officer and spokesperson at recruitment and admission events, and at other venues in the absence of the VPEM. Admissions Operations Oversees application review and selection processes, ensuring consistent, holistic, and mission-aligned admission decisions. Administers and ensures adherence to institutional admission policies, procedures, and deadlines. Oversees major admission projects as assigned by the VPEM. Professional Expectations: Uphold and model the mission, vision, and values of the College in all professional endeavors. Adhere to the policies and procedures of the College. Maintains confidentiality, professionalism, and student-centered service in actions, communication, and behavior in every aspect of the position. Attends and completes any required training, certifications, or other professional development relevant to enrollment leadership and higher education best practices. Requirements: Required Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated success in leading recruitment strategy and achieving enrollment goals in a competitive higher education environment. Strong interpersonal, leadership, and change management skills with the ability to motivate and empower teams. Expertise in CRM systems (e.g., Slate, Salesforce, etc.), enrollment analytics, and communication planning. Capacity to interpret and present data clearly to stakeholders and use analytics to drive decision-making. Excellent verbal, written, and presentation skills tailored to diverse audiences (students, families, faculty, trustees). Valid driver's license and willingness to travel regionally and nationally as needed. Required Experience & Education: Bachelor's degree required; master's degree preferred. Minimum of five years of progressive experience in a college/university admissions office with a record of increasing leadership responsibility. Proven supervisory experience developing and managing a high-performing, cohesive team. Strong acumen with technology, report writing, and PowerPoint presentations. Advanced experience with CRM system use, data analytics, and integrated enrollment marketing is preferred. Additional Information: Physical Requirements: Primarily sedentary work in an office setting. The ability to navigate to various buildings on campus for meetings, training, and other College gatherings. Use of office equipment, including computers, printers, and copiers, with lifting of less than 20lb occasionally to fill machines or move files. Occasional travel for recruitment and professional conferences that may require lifting and transporting presentation equipment and materials. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
    },
    "https://marietta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=188976": {
      "title": "Clinical Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Marietta College\nJob Posting: Clinical Athletic Trainer Marietta College \n\tJob Posting: Clinical Athletic Trainer Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Clinical Athletic Trainer Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Marietta, OH Posted: Jun 6, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 188976 Share About Marietta College: For nearly two centuries, Marietta College has embraced its commitment to serving young adults seeking to better their lives and to turn their life's passions into actionable good in the world. Committed to a contemporary liberal arts education and home to the 16th oldest chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, Marietta offers more than 40 undergraduate programs as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies, Sustainability Leadership, and Psychology. At Marietta, students learn from talented faculty members who are respected in their fields and wholly dedicated to teaching the next generation of leaders. Our professors share their knowledge with students and challenge them to develop their skillsets through serious research, experiential opportunities, and internships. Every student completes Marietta's rigorous General Education Curriculum, which builds strong communication skills and exposes students to new ideas and interests. Our varsity athletic teams compete in NCAA Division III and against some of the best in the nation as a member of the Ohio Athletic Conference and Mid-Atlantic Rowing Conference. Marietta has won six national championships and 64 conference titles, including an OAC-record 46 baseball titles. More than 26,000 living members of The Long Blue Line proudly support their alma mater and help current students gain internships and connections into their chosen industries. This support, in addition to the vibrant growth on campus, is one of the reasons why The Chronicle of Higher Education named Marietta College one of the Great Colleges to Work For. The College sits on 90 picturesque acres in Marietta, Ohio, located just blocks from a historic downtown and the Ohio River. For more information about the College, please visit marietta.edu. Job Description: Provide exceptional health care delivery to athletic programs by promoting holistic student-athlete success and experiences through prevention evaluation, programming for rehabilitation, self-care and wellness. Set athletic training clinic times and home event coverage allows for work/life balance of the staff. This position typically falls in the salary range of $55,000-$58,000 for a 10-month position. Essential Functions of the Position: Work in cooperation with the Head Athletic Trainer in all aspects of the health care of the student-athletes, such as evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of injuries incurred by the intercollegiate student-athletes. Provide onsite care and management of injuries and illnesses including prevention, evaluation, management and rehabilitation. Assess risk of injury, self-care implementation and overall wellness promotion. Complete electronic documentation of patient encounters into PyraMed (EMR). Execute medical care for student-athletes per sports medicine standard operating procedures. Coordinate and implement injury prevention programs and customized preventative strategies and programs to each patient. Collaborate with campus partners and athletic department staff regarding the safety and well-being of student athletes. Communicate with physicians and coaching staff regarding the injury status of athletes. Provide medical care during open clinic times and home athletic events. Travel to away contests as determined by Head Athletic Trainer. Requirements: Required Skills and Abilities: Excellent verbal and written communication. Proficient use of athletic training supplies and equipment, therapeutic modalities, computer, and software. Ability to manage several injuries at one time during an athletic event while maintaining a calm demeanor and providing professional care. Demonstrated teamwork mindset prioritizing the student athlete at all times. Required Experience & Education: Bachelor's degree in athletic training or in a related field Certified athletic trainer Ohio OTPTAT Board Licensure Current CPR for Professional Rescuer/BLS Additional Information: Physical Requirements: Ability to work in a variety of indoor/outdoor settings dependent on the sporting event assigned. This could include cold/hot temperatures and rain or snow. Ability to lift a patient with assistance from coaches or other support staff. Occasional stretching, twisting, grasping, pulling, and other semi-strenuous activities while treating a student athlete. Ability to respond quickly to student's injuries during athletic events with the proper medical supplies and safety protection readily available. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. All applications/resumes must be submitted through this online process. We regret that we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted by mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please be sure to provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating your application materials have been received. Marietta College is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Marietta College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, gender orientation, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, religion, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed service member status, political affiliation, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Marietta College 215 Fifth Street, Marietta, OH 45750"
